2026-10-07|Maximum Path Sum Between Two Leaf Nodes

Question
Given the root of a binary tree, find the maximum possible path sum between any two leaf nodes. If the tree has fewer than two leaf nodes, return `-1`.

Approach

1. Use DFS to calculate the maximum root-to-leaf path sum for every subtree.

2. For each node, recursively calculate:
   - The maximum path sum from the current node down to a leaf in the left subtree.
   - The maximum path sum from the current node down to a leaf in the right subtree.

3. If both left and right subtrees exist, the current node can be the highest point of a path connecting two leaves.

4. The path sum through the current node is:
   `leftSum + node->data + rightSum`

5. Update the global maximum with this value.

6. Return to the parent the best single-side path:
   `node->data + max(leftSum, rightSum)`

7. If a node has only one child, it cannot form a leaf-to-leaf path through both sides. We simply continue through the existing child.

8. Keep a count of the number of leaves. If fewer than two leaves exist, return `-1`.

9. Time complexity is O(n), because every node is visited once.

10. Space complexity is O(h), where `h` is the height of the tree, due to the DFS recursion stack.

Solution
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

struct Node {
    int data;
    Node* left;
    Node* right;

    Node(int val) {
        data = val;
        left = nullptr;
        right = nullptr;
    }
};

class Solution {
public:
    long long ans;
    int leafCount;

    long long dfs(Node* root) {
        if (root == nullptr) {
            return 0;
        }

        if (root->left == nullptr && root->right == nullptr) {
            leafCount++;
            return root->data;
        }

        long long leftSum = dfs(root->left);
        long long rightSum = dfs(root->right);

        if (root->left != nullptr && root->right != nullptr) {
            ans = max(ans, leftSum + root->data + rightSum);

            return root->data + max(leftSum, rightSum);
        }

        if (root->left != nullptr) {
            return root->data + leftSum;
        }

        return root->data + rightSum;
    }

    long long maxPathSum(Node* root) {
        ans = LLONG_MIN;
        leafCount = 0;

        dfs(root);

        if (leafCount < 2) {
            return -1;
        }

        return ans;
    }
};

int main() {
    Node* root = new Node(1);

    root->left = new Node(2);
    root->right = new Node(3);

    root->left->left = new Node(4);
    root->left->right = new Node(5);

    root->right->left = new Node(6);
    root->right->right = new Node(7);

    Solution obj;

    cout << obj.maxPathSum(root) << endl;

    return 0;
}
